values ('a5b6c7d8-9e0f-4b15-8c45-5d6e7f8a9b55', 'ethnographic-area-studies', 'Ethnographic Area Studies', 'Students ask what a region is, who defines it, and how ethnography can study place without freezing cultures into bounded containers. They build historical depth for contemporary cases, design responsible regionally informed research, and analyze colonialism, language and identity, kinship and personhood, symbolic life, political economy, mobility, land and climate, and governance without reducing culture to policy. The course adds comparative and multi-sited analysis, ethics and representation, and a regional research capstone.');

